    </period>
   </indicator>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="2">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Completeness of reporting: Percentage of expected monthly reports (for the reporting period) that are actually received.</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">This indicator will measure the completeness of submission of reports into the HMIS. To track reporting, every MMLL report (paper based) should be submitted to the provincial office from the end of the month to 15th of the following month. 

Data Source: Malaria Annual Report (NVBCDP) and National Surveillance Data
Numerator: Number of expected monthly report (for the reporting period) that are actually received.
Denominator: Total number of expected monthly reports for the reporting period. 

Population figures:&#xa0;&#xa0;There were 318 functioning Health Facilities in 2022 (3,816 expected reports annually). 
In 2022, out of 3,816 expected monthly reports, 62.9% (2,402) monthly facility reports were received.  

Achievement by Province:
- Torba which has 30 health facilities had a reporting completeness of 25% (89/ 360) in 2022
- Shefa which has 59 health facilities had a reporting completeness of 87% (616/ 708) in 2022
- Malampa which has 59 health facilities had a reporting completeness of 85% (599/ 708) in 2022
- Sanma which has 67 health facilities had a reporting completeness of 53% (423/ 804) in 2022                                                                                                             
- Penama which has 70 health facilities had a reporting completeness of 50% (416 /840) in 2022                                                                                                             
- Tafea which has 38 health facilities had a reporting completeness of 56% (259/ 462) in 2022
The two provinces of Malampa and Shefa achieved over 85% report coverage and reached the target of 85%. Plans will be in place for other 4 provinces (Penama, Sanma, Tafea and Torba) to improve in 2024-2026.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline value="62.92" year="2023"></baseline>
