   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of insecticide-treated nets distributed to populations at risk of malaria transmission through mass campaigns</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">his indicator will enable to track progress and performance in ITN mass distribution, and whether ITNs have got to the population at risk on schedule. Mass campaign is done between Q2 and Q3 before the rainy season in selected areas .  Mass campaigns are conducted every three years at the village level. The target coverage rate for these mass distributions has historically been 1.25 people per net, in line with WHO standards to achieve 100% coverage. However, household size according to the 2020 Census indicates that a larger number was warranted per household, especially in Penama, Torba, Malampa and Shefa to ensure coverage for the whole household.

Data Source:  Malaria Annual Report (NVBCDP ) and National Surveillance Data
Numerator: Number of insecticide-treated nets distributed to populations at risk of malaria transmission through mass campaigns.
